# This file contains a list of files that will be excluded from Shopify CLI
# operations such as push, pull, dev, etc.
#
# Examples:
#
# Ignore a specific file:
#   templates/product.json
#
# Ignore templates with a wildcard pattern:
#   templates/*.json
#
# Ignore templates and sections with a regular expression:
#   /(templates|sections)/.*\.json/

# Local setup tooling, not part of the theme
setup-store.mjs
seed-data/*

# Merchant settings live in the store, not in this repo.
#
# This file holds every value chosen in the theme editor: the uploaded logo
# and favicon, the palette, the WhatsApp links, the dispatch wording. Pushing
# it overwrites all of that with whatever the repo happens to hold, which
# silently deletes uploaded images. Ignoring it means a code push changes code
# and leaves the shop's own settings alone.
#
# New settings added to settings_schema.json still work: Shopify falls back to
# the schema default for any key the store has not got a value for yet.
config/settings_data.json

# A pulled-down copy of the live theme, used to rescue content the shop's
# own editor created before a push overwrites it. Never pushed back up.
live-snapshot/*
